This document serves as the master record for the **Vite + TypeScript** migration of the Footprint Chart platform. It completely replaces the vanilla HTML workflow, introducing a strict, modular, and extensible architecture required to support official TradingView Lightweight Charts plugins (e.g., native Moving Average, Median Price).

---

## 1. System Architecture & Paths

The project has been migrated from a single vanilla HTML file into a modern Vite + TypeScript environment.

*   **Root Project Directory**: `/home/hasibrahmat2/lightweight-charts-master/`
*   **TypeScript Environment Root**: `/home/hasibrahmat2/lightweight-charts-master/indicator-examples/`
*   **Vite Public Directory (Data Store)**: `/home/hasibrahmat2/lightweight-charts-master/indicator-examples/public/`
    *   *All static JSON data (`*_1d.json`, `*_5m.json`, `screener_data.json`) must reside here so the Vite dev server can serve them at the root `fetch('/...')` path.*
*   **Main Application Source**: `/home/hasibrahmat2/lightweight-charts-master/indicator-examples/src/my-footprint-ts/`
    *   `index.html`: The HTML layout (Screener, Toolbar, Chart Container).
    *   `main.ts`: The core TypeScript logic binding the UI, charts, orderflow footprint plugin, and indicator plugins.
    *   `style.css`: The UI styling, completely cloned from Stockbit's aesthetic (Inter font, scrollable tabs, soft UI).

---

## 2. Setting Up the Environment & Tools

### A. Dependencies Installation
To run the TypeScript environment, Node.js and NPM are required. We rely on the `indicator-examples` Vite template provided by TradingView, with our custom additions.

```bash
cd /home/hasibrahmat2/lightweight-charts-master/indicator-examples
# Install standard dependencies
npm install

# Install the Orderflow (Footprint) Plugin natively
npm install lightweight-orderflow-charts
```

### B. Starting the Development Server
To launch the platform, use the Vite dev server. The `--host` flag ensures it is accessible from outside environments if needed.

```bash
cd /home/hasibrahmat2/lightweight-charts-master/indicator-examples
npm run dev -- --host
```
*Access the platform via:* `http://localhost:5174/src/my-footprint-ts/`

