## AF. Interactive Legend Hide/Show & Remove Parity for Drawing Overlays (Parallel Channel, Trendlines, Auto S/R)

- **Problem & Motivation**:
  - Technical analysis drawing overlays—specifically **Automated Parallel Channels** (corridor fill, basic trendline, channel line, midline, $A_n/B_n/C_n$ touch markers, and status badge), **Automated Trendlines**, and **Auto S/R**—can populate extensive visual geometry that temporarily obstructs candlestick and footprint details.
  - Technical indicators (`MA 20`, `Median`, etc.) had dedicated `.ind-actions-group` buttons in `#indicators-legend-container` (`👁` hide/show, `🗑` remove). Drawing overlays lacked this control, requiring users to look at dense charts without a fast toggle.
- **Interactive Legend Architecture (`#indicators-legend-container`)**:
  - Whenever an overlay tool is activated from `#tv-left-toolbar`, individual interactive rows are generated for EACH active directional channel and trendline:
    1. `overlay_channel_up`: Displays `Up-Channel`, teal color (`#26A69A`), touch count (`${totalTouches}x Touches`, `Breakout`, `Weakening`, `Broken`, or `Hidden`), and `.ind-actions-group` (`👁` / `🚫`, `🗑`).
    2. `overlay_channel_down`: Displays `Down-Channel`, direction color (`#EF5350` / `#2962FF` / `#787b86`), touch/acceleration status (`Bearish Accel`, `Breakout`, `Weakening`, `Broken`, or `Hidden`), and `.ind-actions-group` (`👁` / `🚫`, `🗑`).
    3. `overlay_trendline_up` & `overlay_trendline_down`: Displays `Up-Trendline` / `Down-Trendline` with their respective touches and actions.
    4. `overlay_sr`: Displays `Auto S/R`, green theme color, status (`Active` or `Hidden`), and `.ind-actions-group` (`👁` / `🚫`, `🗑`).
- **Independent Per-Direction Filtering**:
  - Eliminates channel clutter when stocks (e.g. `AKSI`) possess both an ascending recovery corridor (Up-Channel) and a preceding descending consolidation corridor (Down-Channel):
    - Clicking `👁` on `Down-Channel` hides the entire Down-Channel geometry (corridor fill, basic trendline, channel line, midline, touch badges $C_5..C_{12}$, and Bearish Accel badge) from the chart, leaving ONLY the clean `Up-Channel` visible!
    - Clicking `👁` on `Up-Channel` hides the Up-Channel, leaving ONLY the `Down-Channel` visible!
    - Both can be toggled independently without affecting each other.
- **Interactive Action Behaviors**:
  - **Hide / Show (`👁` / `🚫`)**:
    - Toggling the eye button flips individual visibility (`channelUpVisible`, `channelDownVisible`, `trendlineUpVisible`, `trendlineDownVisible`, `srVisible`).
    - When hidden:
      - Filtered out from `visibleChannels = channels.filter(...)` and cleared from both `nativeCandles` and `footprintSeries`.
      - Legend row applies `.hidden-state` (dimmed opacity 0.45).
      - Status text switches to `Hidden`.
      - Eye icon changes to `🚫` with tooltip `"Show"`.
      - Actions group remains visible on hidden rows (`.ind-legend-row.hidden-state .ind-actions-group { display: flex; }`) so users can unhide with 1 click.
    - When restored:
      - Re-rendered immediately on the canvas with full geometry and badges.
      - Legend row returns to full opacity (1.0).
      - Status text updates with active touch diagnostics.
      - Eye icon reverts to `👁` with tooltip `"Hide"`.
    - Persisted in `localStorage` keys: `user_auto_channel_up_visible`, `user_auto_channel_down_visible`, `user_auto_trendline_up_visible`, `user_auto_trendline_down_visible`, `user_auto_sr_visible`.
  - **Remove (`🗑`)**:
    - 1-click removal completely deactivates the specified direction or tool.
    - Automatically unchecks and removes the `active` class from the corresponding `#tv-left-toolbar` button if all channels/trendlines are removed.
    - Persists state to `localStorage`.
- **Two-Way State Synchronization**:
  - Left-sidebar toolbar button clicks (`#auto-channel-btn`, `#auto-trendline-btn`, `#auto-sr-btn`) immediately insert or remove all corresponding directional rows in the legend and resets their visibility to visible.
  - Top-left legend actions (`👁`, `🗑`) immediately update the chart canvas and local storage.
  - Seamlessly survives timeframe switching (`1m`..`1Y`), symbol search, and arithmetic/logarithmic price scale toggles.
- **Verification & TypeScript Build**:
  - `npm run build` (`tsc`): 0 errors, exit code 0.

