## 37. 500-Stock Watchlist Batch Ingestion, Account Clean-Up & Real-Time Alert Engine Standards

- **User Requirements & Context**:
  - User explored whether `stockbit_intraday_scraper.py` could be run at 500 req/s to monitor hundreds of stocks for technical alerts.
  - Clarified architectural limits: single-threaded synchronous scripts cannot hit 500 req/s, and doing so would trigger immediate Cloudflare WAF bans (`HTTP 429` / account termination).
  - Clarified core user requirement: monitor **511 stocks** from `ihsg_list.csv` for **Demand Zone entries**, **Key Support tests**, and **Resistance breakouts/trendline touches**, with active monitoring and continuous status reports.
- **Stockbit API Reverse-Engineering & Validation**:
  - Discovered Stockbit's official Watchlist REST API suite:
    - `GET https://exodus.stockbit.com/watchlist`: Lists user watchlists.
    - `POST https://exodus.stockbit.com/watchlist`: Creates a new watchlist (`{"name": "..."}`).
    - `DELETE https://exodus.stockbit.com/watchlist/{id}`: Deletes custom watchlists.
    - `GET https://exodus.stockbit.com/watchlist/search/company?keyword={sym}&page=1&watchlist_id={id}`: Resolves stock ticker to Stockbit internal `company_id`.
    - `POST https://exodus.stockbit.com/watchlist/{id}/company/item`: Adds stock via JSON `{"company_id": "<id>"}`.
    - `GET https://exodus.stockbit.com/order-trade/market-mover?mover_type=...`: Official Market Movers endpoint returning 50 top gainers/volume/turnover stocks.
- **Account Clean-Up & 511-Stock Population**:
  - Automatically cleaned 10 legacy empty watchlists (`top gainer 16 juli`, `S2`, `S3`, `S4`, `T1`, `T2`, `T3`, `T4`, `T5`, `MMA`).
  - Created clean target watchlist: **`IHSG 500`** (`Watchlist ID: 17872855`).
  - Executed `populate_watchlist.py` across all 511 stocks from `ihsg_list.csv`:
    - Resolved all company IDs and saved permanent offline lookup to `stockbit_company_ids.json`.
    - Added 511 / 511 stocks into `IHSG 500` on Stockbit's server (`HTTP 200`).
- **Single-Request 500-Stock Batch Ingestion (`GET /watchlist/17872855?limit=500`)**:
  - Stockbit allows and enforces a maximum limit parameter of 500 (`"Limit harus 500 atau kurang;"`).
  - **1 Single Request**: `GET https://exodus.stockbit.com/watchlist/17872855?limit=500` returns the entire 500-stock universe in ~0.25 seconds.
  - Returned payload schema per item: `symbol`, `last` (live current price), `change`, `percent` (% change), `previous` (prev close), `volume` (in shares), `orderbook` (`bid`, `offer`), `notations`, `uma`, and `prices` (intra-day price history sparkline array).
  - Enables polling the entire 500-stock universe every 30s at just **0.033 requests/second** (1 request per 30 seconds), completely eliminating rate limit risks.
- **S/R & Demand Zone Alert Engine Architecture**:
  - **Pre-Calculated Daily Levels**: Demand Zones, Key Supports, and Resistances are computed once per session from historical daily bars (`data/*.csv` / `_1d.json`).
  - **Instant Memory Scanning**: The incoming 500-stock batch quotes are matched against target levels in an $O(1)$ memory lookup (<0.1ms).
  - **Active Lifecycle Tracker & Hotlist State Machine**:
    - Tagging upon alert trigger: moves stock into the **Active Monitored** queue with entry price, zone boundary, invalidation level, and timer (e.g. 4 hours, multi-day).
    - Periodic Heartbeats & Milestone Events: reports continuous updates (Bounce confirmation $+1\%\dots+2\%$, Zone holding, Support breakdown/invalidation, or Target resistance hit).

