## 53. Strict Real-Touch Support Trigger (Removal of ±2 Ticks Noise) & 3-Entry Alert Movement Log for Telegram, Discord & UI Tracking

- **Context & Problem Statement**:
  - Previously, support alerts transitioned to `testing 🎯` when price was within $\pm 2$ ticks of a support line or within $+2$ ticks above a Demand Zone ceiling.
  - Traders noted that $\pm 2$ ticks created excessive false positive alerts ("noise"), alerting prematurely before the price actually touched the support level.
  - Furthermore, traders needed to follow the exact progression of a stock's interaction with support throughout the day without opening the chart:
    1. Exact first time and price when support was touched/tested today.
    2. The previous alert state immediately preceding the current event.
    3. The current alert event.
    4. Ability to dismiss a stock and purge its movement logs once it is no longer interesting.

- **Strict Real-Touch Support Evaluation (Noise Elimination)**:
  - **Demand Zone (Priority 1)**:
    - `price >= zoneBottom && price <= zoneTop`: Strict Real Touch $\rightarrow$ `testing 🎯`.
    - `price > zoneTop`: Safely above Demand Zone (even if $+1$ or $+2$ ticks) $\rightarrow$ `holding 🛡️`.
    - `price < zoneBottom`: Breakdown below Demand Zone floor $\rightarrow$ `broken ⚠️`.
  - **Support Lines (Priority 2 & 3)**:
    - `price === primarySupport.price`: Exact Real Touch $\rightarrow$ `testing 🎯`.
    - `price > primarySupport.price`: Above support (even if $+1$ or $+2$ ticks) $\rightarrow$ `holding 🛡️`.
    - `price < primarySupport.price`: Below support line $\rightarrow$ `broken ⚠️`.

- **3-Entry Alert Movement Log (`AlertMovementLogEntry`)**:
  - Implemented structured movement tracking:
    - `firstTouchLog`: Set on the very first `testing` event of the current trading date (`todayStr`). Persists all day across subsequent alerts unless dismissed or upon day rollover.
    - `prevAlertLog`: Shifted from the previous `currentAlertLog` whenever a new alert triggers. Displays `None (Initial Touch Today)` on the first touch.
    - `currentAlertLog`: The new alert event (`time`, `price`, `changePercent`, `status`, `label`, `date`).
  - **Automated Day Rollover**: Automatically detects trading date changes (`entry.date !== todayStr`) and resets logs cleanly.
  - **Dismiss Action (`.btn-dismiss-follow`)**: Dismisses the stock from Follow Through, ceases tracking, purges movement logs, and removes the card from the UI.

- **Multi-Channel Notification Formatting**:
  - **Discord Webhook (`sendDiscordAlert`)**:
    - Added dedicated embed field: `📋 Movement Log (Today)`:
      - `1️⃣ First: \`10:14:02 WIB\` • Rp 378 (+0.00%) • 🎯 Testing Demand Zone (testing)`
      - `2️⃣ Prev:  \`10:35:10 WIB\` • Rp 384 (+1.59%) • 🛡️ Holding / Bounced Above (holding)`
      - `3️⃣ Now:   \`11:05:00 WIB\` • Rp 372 (-1.59%) • 🎯 Testing Demand Zone (testing)`
  - **Telegram Bot (`sendTelegramAlert`)**:
    - HTML formatted block with automated HTML escaping:
      - `📋 <b>Movement Log (Hari Ini):</b>`
      - `1️⃣ <b>First:</b> <code>10:14:02 WIB</code> • Rp 378 (<code>+0.00%</code>) • 🎯 Testing Demand Zone [TESTING]`
      - `2️⃣ <b>Prev:</b>  <code>10:35:10 WIB</code> • Rp 384 (<code>+1.59%</code>) • 🛡️ Holding / Bounced Above [HOLDING]`
      - `3️⃣ <b>Now:</b>   <code>11:05:00 WIB</code> • Rp 372 (<code>-1.59%</code>) • 🎯 Testing Demand Zone [TESTING]`
  - **Sidebar Drawer Follow Through Card**:
    - Renders `.alert-movement-log` box beneath target support info with live updating 1️⃣ First, 2️⃣ Prev, 3️⃣ Now rows.

- **Verification & Parity Across Bridges**:
  - Synchronized across `indicator-examples/src/my-footprint-ts/main.ts`, `live_trade_bridge.mjs`, `live_trade_bridge.py`, and `mock_trade_emitter.mjs`.
  - Comprehensive unit test `tests/test_realtime_price_alert.mjs` verifying strict real touch (no $\pm 2$ ticks), 3-entry movement progression, day rollover, and dismiss action passes with 100% assertions.
  - TypeScript build (`npm --prefix indicator-examples run build` / `tsc`): 0 errors, exit code 0.

## 54. Bandarmology & Broker Inventory Sidebar Drawer Architecture via IDXEDGEPRO REST APIs (/api/broker-summary & /api/broker-accumulation)

- **Context & Motivation**:
  - Traders require an integrated, real-time Bandarmology drawer directly in the web UI dock (`#dock-broker-summary-btn` with `data-panel="broker-summary"`) to analyze broker accumulation/distribution, Top 1/3/5 concentration, and reconstruct detailed broker inventory positions (% of Free Float, weighted average costs, shortfalls, and implied initial inventory) across arbitrary lookback periods without switching applications or writing batch scripts.

- **IDXEDGEPRO Endpoint Capabilities & Optimizations**:
  - `/api/broker-summary/{code}?start_date={YYYY-MM-DD}&end_date={YYYY-MM-DD}`:
    - Provides up to 25 detailed BUY & 25 SELL levels (`broker_levels`) with `broker_code`, `broker_name`, `bval`, `bvol`, `bavg`, `bfrq`, `sval`, `svol`, `savg`, `sfrq`.
    - Provides broker summary table (`brokers`) with net values (`nval`) and net volumes (`nvol`).
  - `/api/broker-accumulation/{code}?brokers={ALL_IDX_BROKERS}&start_date={YYYY-MM-DD}&end_date={YYYY-MM-DD}`:
    - Bypasses the default 5-broker limit by submitting a comma-separated query of all 87 IDX broker codes.
    - Returns full historical daily accumulation points (`date`, `nval`, `nvol`, `cum_nval`, `bavg`, `savg`) for all active brokers in a single fast HTTP request (~1.0–2.0s).
    - Historical lookback depth extends back to `2020-01-02` (over 1,600 trading days).

- **Strict Terminology & Mathematical Reconstruction Invariants (Section 6 Parity)**:
  - **Terminology Invariant**: Output strictly labeled `"Estimated Position"`, NEVER `"Actual Broker Holdings"`.
  - **Non-Negative Constraint**: Estimated position must NEVER become negative ($\text{position} \ge 0$).
  - **Shortfall & Implied Initial Position**: If selling exceeds tracked inventory ($\text{pos} - \text{sell\_lot} < 0$), $\text{shortfall} = -(\text{pos} - \text{sell\_lot})$, added to `implied_initial_position`, and `position = 0`.
  - **Weighted Average Cost & Sell Invariance**: Sells while holding inventory DO NOT change the average acquisition cost. Buys recalculate weighted average price:
    $$\text{AvgCost}_{\text{new}} = \frac{\text{pos}_{\text{prev}} \times \text{cost}_{\text{prev}} + \text{buy\_lot} \times \text{buy\_price}}{\text{pos}_{\text{prev}} + \text{buy\_lot}}$$
  - When position drops to 0, average cost resets to `null`. Subsequent BUYs restart the cost basis.
  - **% Free Float Calculation**: $\text{Position (lots)} / (\text{listed\_shares} / 100) \times 100\%$, integrated with in-memory `stockMarketCapMap`.
  - **Source Classification**: Tagged as `Observed` (buys only), `Mixed` (buys + shortfalls), `Implied` (shortfalls only), or `None`.

- **Comprehensive Inventory & Bandarmology Metric Definitions**:
  - **1. Cum Net Val (Cumulative Net Value)**:
    - **Formula**: $\text{Cum Net Val} = \sum \text{Buy Value (IDR)} - \sum \text{Sell Value (IDR)}$ across the selected lookback period.
    - **Interpretation**:
      - **Positive (Green, e.g. `+Rp 45.2 B`)**: Fresh capital injection. The broker deployed net Rupiah liquidity into the stock (Net Accumulator).
      - **Negative (Red, e.g. `-Rp 28.5 B`)**: Capital extraction / cash out. The broker pulled Rupiah out of the stock (Net Seller / Distribution).
  - **2. Implied (Implied Initial Position / Shortfall)**:
    - **Formula**: Whenever running inventory drops below zero ($\text{raw\_net} = \text{pos}_{\text{prev}} + \text{buy} - \text{sell} < 0$):
      $$\text{shortfall} = -(\text{pos}_{\text{prev}} + \text{buy} - \text{sell})$$
      $$\text{implied\_initial\_position} += \text{shortfall}$$
      $$\text{position} = 0$$
    - **Why It Exists**: Physical equity cannot be negative ($\text{position} \ge 0$). In any finite observation window (e.g. 1D, 1M, 1Y), sells exceeding observed buys signify shares acquired *prior* to the observation start date (e.g. IPO allotments, founder crossings, or historical accumulation).
    - **Interpretation**:
      - `Implied = 0` (or `-`): All sales were fully covered by shares bought during this observation window.
      - `Implied > 0` (e.g. `50.0K lot`): The broker distributed older, pre-existing inventory held before the observation window.
      - **Post-Sept 28 Short Selling Context**: On short-eligible stocks (LQ45), an implied shortfall after September 28 can also indicate an **active short position** (borrowed and sold shares).
  - **3. Source (Position Source Tag)**:
    - Identifies the origin and pedigree of the broker's current estimated inventory:
      - **`Observed`** (Blue badge): 100% of current inventory was bought *during* the observation window ($\text{implied} = 0, \text{bought} > 0$). Highest certainty; exact acquisition dates and cost basis are verified.
      - **`Mixed`** (Purple badge): The broker distributed pre-existing inventory earlier (shortfall occurred, $\text{implied} > 0$), but subsequently accumulated fresh shares ($\text{bought} > 0$). Represents inventory turnover / re-accumulation.
      - **`Implied`** (Amber badge): The broker only sold pre-existing inventory without meaningful new purchases ($\text{implied} > 0, \text{bought} = 0$). Represents pure historical distribution.
      - **`None`** (Gray badge): Zero remaining inventory ($\text{position} = 0$). Broker either fully exited or was purely day-trading (in-and-out within the same session).

- **Web UI & User Experience**:
  - **Right Dock Integration**: Dedicated 6th icon (`#dock-broker-summary-btn`, briefcase icon) opens drawer mode `'broker-summary'`.
  - **Dual View Modes**:
    1. `Top Summary` View:
       - Bandar Detector pill badge: `Big Accumulation` (🟢), `Normal Accumulation` (🟩), `Neutral` (⬜), `Normal Distribution` (🟧), `Big Distribution` (🔴) based on Top 3 Net vs total turnover ratio.
       - Top 1, Top 3, Top 5 concentration KPI cards with Net Buy/Sell difference and IDR formatting.
       - Side-by-side Top 25 Buyers vs Top 25 Sellers table (Rank, Broker, Lot, Value, Avg Price).
    2. `All Inventory` View:
       - Inventory overview KPI cards: Active Brokers count, Net Accumulating brokers, Top Holder broker & % Float, and Total Inventory Tracked.
       - Full reconstructed broker inventory table: Rank, Broker Code & Name, Estimated Position (Lots), % Free Float, Avg Cost (Rp), Cumulative Net Value (IDR), Implied Initial (Lots), and Source badge.
       - Client-side live text search filtering (`#bs-broker-search-input`) by broker code or name.
  - **Timeframe Selector**: Quick pill buttons for `1D`, `1W`, `1M` (default), `3M`, `YTD`, `1Y`, `All (2020)`, and `Custom 📅` (date range pickers).
  - **Panel Expansion & Ticker Sync**: Seamless toggle between standard 350px and expanded 600px+ width (`#bs-expand-btn`), live refresh (`#bs-refresh-btn`), and auto-reload on chart ticker change.

- **Verification**:
  - Unit tests in `tests/test_broker_position_reconstruction.py`: 13 passed (100%).
  - TypeScript build (`tsc --noEmit` / `npm run build`): 0 errors, exit code 0.

